<span id="A3.T7.2.1.1.1.1.1.1.24" class="ltx_tr">
<span id="A3.T7.2.1.1.1.1.1.1.24.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top">
<span id="A3.T7.2.1.1.1.1.1.1.24.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:455.2pt;">
<span id="A3.T7.2.1.1.1.1.1.1.24.1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.T7.2.1.1.1.1.1.1.24.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">The math problem wants to know how many clips Natalia sold in total. In April, she sold 48. In May, she sold half as many, so she sold 48 / 2 = 24. In total, she sold 48 + 24 = 72. In the problem solving process, the user says that ’half of that, which is 96.’ This is incorrect. The correct number for May should be 24. This is where the first error occurs. Based on the Word-Timestamp information, the word 96 is emitted at second.</span></span>
</span></span></span>
